{
  "fileId": "11",
  "lessons": {
    "11A": {
      "theory": [
        {
          "title": "Past Perfect",
          "text": "had + V3. Показывает, что одно действие произошло раньше другого в прошлом («уже успело случиться»).",
          "examples": [
            {
              "en": "When we arrived, the film had already started.",
              "ru": "Когда мы пришли, фильм уже начался. (сначала начался, потом мы пришли)"
            },
            {
              "en": "I didn't recognise her because she had changed a lot.",
              "ru": "Я не узнал её, потому что она сильно изменилась."
            }
          ],
          "tip": "Сравни: When I got home, my wife cooked dinner (сначала пришёл, потом она готовила). / When I got home, my wife had cooked dinner (ужин уже был готов)."
        }
      ],
      "videos": [
        {
          "title": "Past perfect (B1)",
          "kind": "youtube-search",
          "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=past+perfect+pre-intermediate+lesson"
        }
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "11a-1",
          "type": "gap-fill",
          "instruction": "Complete with the past perfect.",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "When I got to the station, the train ___.",
              "hint": "leave",
              "answers": [
                "had left",
                "'d left"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "She was nervous because she ___ before.",
              "hint": "never fly",
              "answers": [
                "had never flown",
                "'d never flown"
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "I couldn't pay because I ___ my wallet.",
              "hint": "forget",
              "answers": [
                "had forgotten",
                "'d forgotten"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "11a-2",
          "type": "multiple-choice",
          "instruction": "Past simple or past perfect?",
          "items": [
            {
              "question": "When I opened the fridge, someone ___ my cake.",
              "options": [
                "ate",
                "had eaten"
              ],
              "answer": 1
            },
            {
              "question": "He ___ the door and went out.",
              "options": [
                "opened",
                "had opened"
